(vector (map (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "cloud-itonami-isic-5820 flagship promotion (pricing + billing)" "pricing-intel run pricing-intel-20260717-01" "Managed CRM (Starter) Stripe live objects")), (:adr/topic "cloud-itonami-isic-5820-salesforce-replace-flagship"), (:adr/related (vector "adr-2607161745" "adr-2607161620" "adr-2607172500" "cloud-itonami-isic-5820")), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/id "adr-2607172600-cloud-itonami-isic-5820-salesforce-replace-flagship"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-17"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607172600: cloud-itonami-isic-5820 (Salesforce-replace CRM) -- flagship promotion: pricing-intel run 20260717-01 + Managed CRM (Starter) Stripe live Payment Link\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-17\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (owner directive 2026-07-17: \"salesforce replace \u3092\u512a\u5148\"; agent-executed)\n**Scope**: `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5820` (docs-only child commit), superproject\n`90-docs/pricing-intelligence/`, `90-docs/business/cloud-itonami-vertical-maturity.edn`,\nStripe live account. No actor code changed.\n**Builds on**: ADR-2607161745 (flagship Managed-tier Stripe pattern, \u00a580k/\u6708 portfolio price\npoint), ADR-2607161620 (Stripe go-live, secret-handling procedure), ADR-2607172500\n(kotoba-lang/crm registration, same session)\n\n## Context\n\nOwner directive (2026-07-17): prioritize the Salesforce-replace vertical alongside the existing\nflagship trio (6399/6310/7810). `cloud-itonami-isic-5820` already implements the\nSalesforce/HubSpot-class governed CRM (RevOps-LLM sealed behind SubscriptionGovernor:\ndiscount-authority, entitlement-scope, stage-sequence, ASC 606/IFRS 15 revrec; append-only audit\nledger) with a live product face at itonami.cloud/isic-5820/. Three gaps kept it out of the\nflagship cohort: (1) `kotoba-lang/crm` unregistered (fixed by ADR-2607172500), (2) zero\npricing-intelligence coverage (no CRM competitor observations existed; isic-5820 absent from both\nthe 30-vertical real dataset and the 87 pricing-oracle predictions), (3) no billing object -- an\noperator lead had nothing to convert against.\n\n## Decision\n\n### 1. pricing-intelligence run `pricing-intel-20260717-01` (obs seq 131-135, rec seq 136)\n\nFive real competitors surveyed 2026-07-17, all per-seat: Salesforce Sales Cloud ($25/$100/$175/\n$350/$550 per user/mo, Starter->Agentforce 1 Sales), HubSpot Sales Hub (from $7/seat/mo annual;\nPro $90 + $1,500 onboarding; Enterprise $150 + $3,500 onboarding), Pipedrive (Lite $14 / Growth\n$39 / Premium $59 / Ultimate $79 seat/mo annual), Zoho CRM ($14/$23/$40/$52 user/mo annual),\nMicrosoft Dynamics 365 Sales ($65/$105/$150 user/mo yearly). Vendor pages fetched directly where\npossible (HubSpot, Zoho, Microsoft); Salesforce and Pipedrive vendor pages returned HTTP 403 to\nthe fetcher, list prices cross-verified same day via aggregators -- noted honestly per-observation\nin the ledger. Recommended band: **\u00a550,000-150,000/\u6708 flat, unlimited seats** -- a typical 5-rep\nSMB team's real per-seat spend spans ~\u00a517k-131k/\u6708 at ~\u00a5150/$, and the governed layer (structural\nblocks, not configurable approval workflows) carries the top of the band. Same managed-tenant\nrange independently validated for 6399/6310/7810 -- one consistent portfolio price point.\n\n### 2. Stripe live objects -- Managed CRM (Starter), \u00a580,000/\u6708 flat\n\nSame account and procedure as ADR-2607161745 (`op read` into a shell variable once, value never\nechoed; Idempotency-Key on every call; flat `recurring[interval]=month` Price, no Billing Meter):\n\n- Product `prod_UtpXavUeUTwhYQ` \"cloud-itonami Managed CRM (Starter)\"\n- Price `price_1Tu1sTBcblPoapUJ2BHebZEv` (JPY 80,000/month recurring, unlimited seats)\n- Payment Link `plink_1Tu1sTBcblPoapUJzEbMMgKS` -> https://buy.stripe.com/4gM28q88r4pyaGIdIzbMQ0e\n\nPublished in the child repo `docs/business-model.md` under Revenue Model (server-side merge\n`f2ba51d21d74`); west pin advanced `3a3f1685374f` -> `f2ba51d21d74` via `--entry`, verify OK.\n\n**Bookkeeping deviation from ADR-2607161745**: `op item create` (and `op item get`) failed with\n`authorization timeout` (known op-CLI write-path issue, cf. CLAUDE.md fleet-db kagi note), so no\n1Password item was created -- **this ADR is the authoritative record of the object IDs** (IDs and\nthe Payment Link URL are not secrets; the URL is published in the repo anyway).\n\n### 3. Flagship cohort + dogfood direction (no code in this ADR)\n\n- `cloud-itonami-vertical-maturity.edn` cohort row updated: 5820 leaves \"Software/IT 5820/620x\n  local checkout missing\" and gets its own flagship row (Design 5 / Impl-core 4 / Impl-product 4 /\n  Business 2 -- same Business formula as 6399/6310/7810: payment link live, no paid org yet).\n- Dogfood: operate cloud-itonami's own managed-tier sales motion (7810/6310/6399 leads) inside\n  the 5820 actor itself; 7310 (advertising) / 7320 (market research) actor cores as the growth\n  engine feeding that pipeline. \"The pipeline you are looking at is our real pipeline\" is the\n  demo. This gives 5820 grounding/validation while fixing the portfolio's weakest dimension\n  (distribution=2).\n\n## Consequences / open gates\n\n- First-paid-org gate unchanged: `hyp/itonami-smb-pay` (external-paid >= 1) stays `measuring`.\n- **E2E checkout verification remains open** (inherited from ADR-2607161620; still skipped) --\n  close it before driving any real lead into checkout, now for 4 flagship links.\n- Sibling actors (marketing-automation hub, customer-service hub) stay roadmap-only per the\n  child repo's narrowing discipline; 6201/6202/6209 remain non-flagship.\n"), (:adr/deciders (vector "Jun Kawasaki")), (:adr/date "2026-07-17"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2607172600: cloud-itonami-isic-5820 (Salesforce-replace CRM) -- flagship promotion: pricing-intel run 20260717-01 + Managed CRM (Starter) Stripe live Payment Link"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))